From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kc <barteo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:48:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse the symbols of generated files whose text is unchanged

After each round, registerGeneratedFiles visited every declaration of
every file the round generated, to record the symbols it defines. A
daemon that runs KSP again generates most of those files with the same
text as the run before, and on the Hilt bench that visit (through the
files' Java classes and their members) took about 1 ms a run.

The symbols depend only on a file's text, so the last text and symbols
of each generated file are kept for the process, and a file generated
again with the same text gets the kept symbols. KSP_NO_SYMBOL_REUSE=1
collects them every time; KSP_SYMBOL_VERIFY=1 collects them every time
and fails if they differ from the kept ones.
---
